.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbc
is the boot-configuration and boot-control companion to the Leon bootloader.
It edits the boot configuration consumed by the bootloader, runs the
full-screen keyboard-driven boot-manager menu (a pure-Rust ratatui app, no
embedded Python), stages the ESP tree, and reports the boot volume layout.
It reuses the shared host-side discovery and geometry modules from the
.B lbt
library; the image builders remain in
.BR lbt (1).
.PP
The `lbc tui` menu mirrors the bootloader's runtime experience by exporting
live framebuffer + BGRT geometry and discovered boot entries to environment
variables. It also uses the shared boot config and geometry models so host-side
staging and menu behavior remain consistent with the UEFI boot path.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS tui
Launch the Leon boot-manager menu: a full-screen, keyboard-driven ratatui app
that mirrors what the bootloader renders at boot. Before it runs, lbc exports
the live framebuffer + BGRT geometry, the discovered boot entries, and the boot
config as
.I LEON_*
environment variables
(\fILEON_FB_WIDTH\fR, \fILEON_FB_HEIGHT\fR, \fILEON_FB_STRIDE\fR,
\fILEON_FB_FORMAT\fR, \fILEON_BOOT_ENTRIES\fR with one
\fIlabel<TAB>path\fR per line). Entries normally come from live discovery
(.efi PE/COFF binaries and EFI-stub ELF kernels on mounted ESPs and under
`/boot`), or from the entries file written by the bootloader; geometry may be
absent (no framebuffer) — the menu shows a friendly placeholder state.
.PP
The menu uses the full keymap: arrows and
.I hjkl
to move, PgUp/PgDn, Home/End, \fI1-9\fR/\fI0\fR to jump to the nth entry,
.I /
to search with
.I n
/
.I N
for next/previous match and
.I p
to un-filter,
.I d
to toggle the detail panel,
.I h
to toggle help,
.I r
to refresh, Enter or space or
.I s
for a boot preview, and
.I q
/ Esc / Ctrl+C to quit.
.SS config
.TP
.B config get \fI[key]\fR
Print one boot config key, or all keys when omitted.
.TP
.B config set \fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
Set a boot config key. Supported keys:
.IR timeout ,
.IR default_entry ,
.IR theme ,
.IR splash ,
.IR entries_file
(the former must be
.B true
or
.BR false ).
The new value is written to
.I ~/.config/leon/boot.toml
and mirrored onto every mounted EFI System Partition as
.IR \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml ,
which is what the bootloader reads at boot.
.TP
.B config list
Print the entire resolved boot configuration.
.TP
.B config reset
Reset the boot config to defaults.
.TP
.B config path
Print the resolved host boot config path.
.SS boot
.TP
.B boot stage \fR[\fB\-\-dest \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-arch \fIarch\fR]
Stage a ready-to-boot ESP tree (bootloader at
.IR \eEFI\eBOOT ,
EFI-stub kernel at
.IR \eEFI\eleon\ekernel.efi ,
boot config mirrored) under
.I build/esp
or
.IR \-\-dest ,
mirroring the Makefile
.B stage
target. Requires
.B "lbt build all"
outputs.
.TP
.B boot info
Report the boot volume layout: host config path, detected ESPs, and the paths
the bootloader expects on the boot volume.
.TP
.B boot once \fIname\fR
Validate a boot entry and describe how to boot it a single time from the
boot-manager menu.
.TP
.B boot upload \fR[\fB\-\-vol \fIpath\fR]
Mirror the boot config onto a mounted ESP (every detected ESP when
.IR \-\-vol
is omitted).
.SS default
.TP
.B default get
Print the configured default boot entry.
.TP
.B default set \fIname\fR
Set the default boot entry label.
.SS entries
.TP
.B entries list
List discovered boot entries.
.TP
.B entries get \fIname\fR
Resolve one boot entry label to its path.
.TP
.B entries count
Count discovered boot entries.
.SS find
.TP
.B find esps
List detected EFI System Partitions.
.TP
.B find entries \fIname\fR
Find boot entries by label.
.SS geometry
.TP
.B geometry show
Show live framebuffer + BGRT geometry.
.TP
.B geometry bgr
Show BGRT logo geometry.
.SS keymap
.TP
.B keymap show
Print the boot-manager keymap.
.SS profile
.TP
.B profile save \fIprofile\fR
Save the current boot config as a named profile.
.TP
.B profile list
List saved boot-config profiles.
.TP
.B profile load \fIprofile\fR
Restore a boot config from a named profile.
.TP
.B profile delete \fIprofile\fR
Delete a saved boot-config profile.
.SS status
Print the boot configuration status: path, keys, saved profiles, and ESPs.
.SS help
.TP
.B help all
Print the full command reference.
.TP
.B help tree
Print the command tree.
.TP
.B help command \fIname\fR
Describe one command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/leon/boot.toml
Host copy of the boot configuration (timeout, default_entry, theme, splash,
entries_file) written by
.BR "lbc config set" .
If absent,
.B config get
falls back to the copy on a mounted ESP.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml
The copy the bootloader actually reads, kept on the boot volume (ESP) and
validated by it at every boot; a missing or broken file simply yields
defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.config/leon/profiles/*.toml
Saved boot-config profiles managed by
.BR "lbc profile" .
